  <compounddef id="structllvm_1_1_first_index_of_type" kind="struct" language="C++" prot="public">
    <compoundname>llvm::FirstIndexOfType</compoundname>
    <templateparamlist>
      <param>
        <type>typename <ref refid="class_t" kindref="compound">T</ref></type>
      </param>
      <param>
        <type>typename...</type>
        <declname>Us</declname>
        <defname>Us</defname>
      </param>
    </templateparamlist>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Find the first index where a type appears in a list of types. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>FirstIndexOfType&lt;T, Us...&gt;::value is the first index of T in Us.</para>
<para>Typically only meaningful when it is otherwise statically known that the type pack has no duplicate types. This should be guaranteed explicitly with static_assert(TypesAreDistinct&lt;Us...&gt;::value).</para>
<para>It is a compile-time error to instantiate when T is not present in Us, i.e. if is_one_of&lt;T, Us...&gt;::value is false. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
